  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-466926\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block\" stepid=\"466926\" steptype=\"tutorial\" contentid=\"1658\">\n            <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                <div class=\"stepName\">\n                    <a id=\"stepAnchor-466926\" class=\"stepAnchor\" name=\"step-15\">Modeling Assumptions</a>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"466926\">?</div>\n            </div> \n\n            <p>In this topic, we made the following assumptions:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>All objects are treated like a <strong>particle</strong>, a small point with no length, width, or height.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>All objects move vertically down in a straight line, so acceleration due to gravity is taken as positive.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>The only acceleration the objects have is due to gravity, and any other forces (such as wind resistance) are negligible.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n        </div>",
